[Fact]
public void DisplayNameReadsAttributesCorrectly()
{
    var appElement = Browser.MountTestComponent<DisplayNameComponent>();

    // Check that DisplayAttribute.Name is displayed
    var displayNameLabel = appElement.FindElement(By.Id("product-name-label"));
    Browser.Equal("Product Name", () => displayNameLabel.Text);

    // Check that DisplayNameAttribute is displayed
    var priceLabel = appElement.FindElement(By.Id("price-label"));
    Browser.Equal("Unit Price", () => priceLabel.Text);

    // Check that DisplayAttribute takes precedence over DisplayNameAttribute
    var stockLabel = appElement.FindElement(By.Id("stock-label"));
    Browser.Equal("Stock Quantity", () => stockLabel.Text);

    // Check fallback to property name when no attributes present
    var descriptionLabel = appElement.FindElement(By.Id("description-label"));
    Browser.Equal("Description", () => descriptionLabel.Text);

    // Check that ResourceType localization works with English resources
    var localizedLabel = appElement.FindElement(By.Id("localized-label"));
    Browser.Equal("Product Name", () => localizedLabel.Text);
}

findings.body:
`ExpressionMemberAccessor` stores `ConcurrentDictionary<Expression, MemberInfo>` as a static field. Razor evaluates `@(() => _product.Name)` on every render, which creates a new expression tree each time. Each `GetOrAdd` call therefore inserts a new entry that is never removed. The expression tree also captures the parent component's closure, so the cache keeps those components alive.

This happens on a normal path. Each time a parent that renders `DisplayName` re-renders, `DisplayName` sees a new `For` reference and calls `GetDisplayName`, which inserts another entry. The cache is only cleared on hot reload.

::diff{file="src/Components/Web/src/Forms/ExpressionMemberAccessor.cs" lines="15-16"}

::callout{type="perf"}
The per-member display name is cheap to compute. The `Expression`-keyed cache is the part that needs to go. The existing `FieldIdentifier` cache is keyed on `(Type, MemberInfo)`, which stays bounded.

::suggestion{file="src/Components/Web/src/Forms/ExpressionMemberAccessor.cs" lines="30-49"}
private static MemberInfo GetMemberInfo<TValue>(Expression<Func<TValue>> accessor)
{
    ArgumentNullException.ThrowIfNull(accessor);

    var accessorBody = accessor.Body;
    if (accessorBody is UnaryExpression unary
        && unary.NodeType == ExpressionType.Convert
        && unary.Type == typeof(object))
    {
        accessorBody = unary.Operand;
    }

    if (accessorBody is not MemberExpression memberExpression)
    {
        throw new ArgumentException(
            $"The provided expression contains a {accessorBody.GetType().Name} which is not supported. " +
            $"Only simple member accessors (fields, properties) of an object are supported.");
    }

    return memberExpression.Member;
}

The PR description says `DisplayName<TValue>` is `public class DisplayName<TValue> : ComponentBase`. The implementation instead implements `IComponent` directly and hand-rolls `Attach` and `SetParametersAsync`. `ValidationMessage<TValue>` and the other form components derive from `ComponentBase`. Users who expect `ComponentBase` members, or who subclass the component, will be surprised. The public API file also records the type as an `IComponent` implementation rather than the documented `ComponentBase`.

If the direct `IComponent` approach is deliberate, say so in the PR description and the XML doc. Otherwise, switch to `ComponentBase`, which also removes the manual `RenderHandle` handling.

::diff{file="src/Components/Web/src/Forms/DisplayName.cs" lines="17-17"}

`RenderAndGetOutput` declares `displayLabelComponentFrame` and never uses it. The helper then picks the first `Text` frame in the batch, so it never checks that the text came from the `DisplayName` component. The test passes because `TestHostComponent` happens to emit no other text, not because the lookup is correct.

`SupportsLocalizationWithResourceType` only reads a static property (`LocalizedDisplayName`). It does not exercise resource lookup, so its name overstates what it proves.

